gify(data); const opts = chartOptions(data); console.log('default export is functio\n93 ERROR Permission to use Bash has been denied because Claude Code is running in don't ask mode. IMPORTANT: You *may* attempt to accomplish this action using other tools that might natural\n97 TEXT The compound shell loop was denied. I'll try a plainer form: a check script in the workspace, run with a single `node` call.\n98 Write check.mjs\n100 Bash node check.mjs\n102 TEXT Production build is clean. Now the development build, which also reports hints such as AX104 for unparsed numeric strings:\n103 Bash node --conditions=development check.mjs\n108 TEXT Zero diagnostics in both builds. As a quick sanity check that `validate` is actually catching things here, a negative control: the same data without `parse: 'number'` should raise hint AX104.\n109 Bash node --conditions=development --input-type=module -e \"import { validate } from 'axylo'; import { chartOptions } from './chart.js'; import { readFileSync } from 'node:fs'; const o = chartOptions(JSON.parse(readFileSync('./data.json','utf8'))); o.y = o.y.map(({ parse, ...f }) => f); for (const d of validate('bar', o)) console.log(d.code, d.level, d.field);\"\n115 TEXT I've written `chart.js`. Its default export `render(element, data)` draws a grouped bar chart titled \"Quarterly sales by region\" into the element you pass and returns the Axylo chart handle. I haven't seen it drawn: charts need a browser and I only had Node. What I could check in Node passed (details below).  **Two problems in `data.json`\n\nclaude-regional-sales-3-HQnAMR\n4 TEXT I'll start by looking at the workspace, docs, and data.\n5 Bash ls -la && find docs -type f | head -100 && cat data.json | head -50\n9 TEXT Notable: the rows are out of order, the values are numeric strings, and the data is in wide format. Let me read the docs.\n10 Bash cat PROMPT.md package.json && ls docs docs/examples | head -200 && ls -R node_modules | head -50\n12 Bash python3 -c \" impor