{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_36","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"nl -ba apps/docs/pages/conformance.md | head -22 && rg -n -i 'verified|coding agent|rehearsal|DX12' apps/docs/pages/stability.md && nl -ba apps/docs/pages/getting-started.md | sed -n '39,53p'\nnl -ba apps/docs/examples/numeric-strings.ts && nl -ba packages/axylo/src/data/values.ts | sed -n '5,62p'\nnl -ba rehearsal/records/release-1e93128/*-codex-daily-revenue-3-*/transcript.jsonl | sed -n '3,6p' | cut -c1-1300\"","aggregated_output":"     1\t# Conformance table\n     2\t\n     3\tAfter this page you know which WCAG 2.2 success criteria the specification cites, what Axylo does for each, what evidence was recorded for them when this site was built, why no test covers the other level A and AA criteria, and what that evidence cannot show.\n     4\t\n     5\tThis page is generated each time the site is built, from the specification's criterion rows and from the report of the acceptance checker. It says only what they record; where they record nothing, it says \"not recorded\". It is not a claim that a page using Axylo conforms: conformance belongs to a whole page, and the page is yours.\n     6\t\n     7\t## What the evidence can and cannot show\n     8\t\n     9\t- **Automated checks only.** The acceptance tests check structure: names, roles, focus order, contrast, sizes and text. They do not show that a person using a screen reader understands a chart.\n    10\t- **No screen-reader rehearsal was done for 1.0.** No screen reader has been run against these charts, so nothing in this documentation says what a screen reader speaks.\n    11\t- **No usability testing with disabled people.** Axylo is built by one person with no access to study participants, and no claim of usability testing with disabled users is made.\n    12\t- **Engines, not browsers.** Browser results are recorded per engine: Chrome, and Firefox and WebKit as built by Playwright. WebKit results are Playwright's WebKit, not Safari. Nothing has been run on a phone.\n    13\t- **Right-to-left pages.** Right-to-left text renders, but the chart's layout is not mirrored.\n    14\t- **Transformed ancestors.** A chart inside a translated or scaled element is exact. Inside a rotated, skewed or mirrored element it draws, but pointing and tooltip placement are wrong; that is not supported in 1.0.\n    15\t\n    16\t## What you must supply\n    17\t\n    18\tAxylo can only describe what it is given. A chart needs a meaningful name (`title`, or `labelledBy` pointing at your heading), series names, units on value fields, and the page's own structure around it. A compact chart fed by `append` has no Pause control, since it has no toolbar: a page that streams into compact tiles must give the reader its own way to pause them (WCAG 2.2.2). [Accessibility](accessibility.md#what-you-must-supply) has the details.\n    19\t\n    20\t## The criteria the specification cites\n    21\t\n    22\t[table: conformance](../../../acceptance/check.mjs)\n23:**What it does not cover.** The chart's internal DOM structure and class names, the custom properties listed as internal, the roles the plot uses to talk to assistive technology (chosen without screen-reader rehearsal, and changeable in a minor release if rehearsal shows a better pattern), and the exact pixels of the drawing.\n27:These are the targets of 1.0 (spec section 2.3). What has been verified so far is listed after the table.\n39:Tested so far, on Linux: the library's acceptance tests in Chrome and in Playwright's builds of Firefox and WebKit (Playwright's WebKit, not Safari), and the distribution tests in Chrome (they install the packed package, also under a Content Security Policy). Safari itself, Edge, Windows, macOS and phones have not been tested. No screen-reader rehearsal was done for 1.0. What the acceptance checker recorded for this revision is on the [conformance page](conformance.md); see also [Accessibility](accessibility.md#what-has-and-has-not-been-verified).\n    39\t[example: lifecycle](../examples/lifecycle.ts)\n    40\t\n    41\t## Daily data: five things to get right\n    42\t\n    43\tThe first chart above has months as calendar dates and numbers as numbers. Data from an API is often less tidy. Here is a daily metric as many back ends send it, and the chart that reads it correctly:\n    44\t\n    45\t[example: daily-sessions](../examples/daily-sessions.ts)\n    46\t\n    47\t1. **Days sent as UTC midnights.** For daily totals sent as `'2026-02-24T00:00:00Z'` (or as epoch milliseconds of a UTC midnight), use `x: { field: 'day', type: 'date' }`. Without it they are instants, shown in the viewer's time zone, so west of UTC each value appears on the day before, with only hint [AX111](diagnostics.md#ax111). Strings such as `'2026-02-24'` need no `type`. See [the three kinds of time](data.md#three-kinds-of-time).\n    48\t2. **Numbers sent as strings.** For decimal strings, use `y: { field: 'sessions', parse: 'number' }`. They are converted to JavaScript numbers, which are exact for integers up to 9,007,199,254,740,991; a larger count is rounded without a warning, so check exact counts with `Number.isSafeInteger` first. A field that mixes numbers and strings is not converted at all. See [numbers sent as strings](data.md#numbers-sent-as-strings).\n    49\t3. **Row order.** Pass rows in any order. Axylo sorts dated rows by x and keeps each value with its own row; categories keep the order in which they first appear.\n    50\t4. **A day with no data.** When you know a day is missing, send it, with `sessions: null`. Axylo can infer a missing day only between two rows of a series that has at least three rows at a regular step, and never before the first row or after the last; with two rows, or an irregular series, the line runs straight across the missing day. See [missing values](data.md#missing-values).\n    51\t5. **A misspelled field.** On error [AX101](diagnostics.md#ax101), compare the field you named with the keys the message lists, which come from your rows, and use the suggested spelling when one is offered. With no rows at all the keys cannot be checked, so the error appears once data arrives. With typed rows in TypeScript the typo does not compile.\n    52\t\n    53\t## What you get without asking\n     1\timport { bar } from 'axylo';\n     2\t\n     3\t// Postgres returns `count(*)` as a string (bigint). Declaring the parse says that is expected.\n     4\tconst rows = [\n     5\t  { day: '2026-03-02', orders: '182' },\n     6\t  { day: '2026-03-03', orders: '205' },\n     7\t  { day: '2026-03-04', orders: '199' },\n     8\t  { day: '2026-03-05', orders: '231' },\n     9\t];\n    10\t\n    11\tbar('#chart', {\n    12\t  title: 'Orders per day',\n    13\t  data: rows,\n    14\t  x: 'day',\n    15\t  y: { field: 'orders', parse: 'number', label: 'Orders' },\n    16\t});\n     5\t\n     6\tconst decimal = /^[+-]?\\d+(?:\\.\\d+)?(?:[eE][+-]?\\d+)?$/;\n     7\texport type ValueMode = 'empty' | 'decimal' | 'other';\n     8\texport type ValueCounts = Record<Exclude<ValueMode, 'empty'>, number>;\n     9\t\n    10\texport function valueMode(value: unknown, column: boolean): ValueMode {\n    11\t  if (value == null || value === '' || (column && typeof value === 'number' && Number.isNaN(value))) return 'empty';\n    12\t  return typeof value === 'string' && decimal.test(value) ? 'decimal' : 'other';\n    13\t}\n    14\t\n    15\texport function inspectValues(table: Table, field: string, included?: (row: number) => boolean): ValueMode {\n    16\t  let mode: ValueMode = 'empty';\n    17\t  for (let i = 0; i < table.length; i++) {\n    18\t    if (included && !included(i)) continue;\n    19\t    const next = valueMode(table.read(i, field), table.isColumnRow(i));\n    20\t    if (next === 'other') return next;\n    21\t    if (next === 'decimal') mode = next;\n    22\t  }\n    23\t  return mode;\n    24\t}\n    25\t\n    26\texport interface Values {\n    27\t  readonly y: Float64Array | Float32Array;\n    28\t  readonly slot: Uint8Array;\n    29\t}\n    30\t\n    31\texport function readValues(\n    32\t  table: Table,\n    33\t  field: ResolvedValueField,\n    34\t  sink: DiagnosticSink,\n    35\t  impute: boolean,\n    36\t  startRow = 0,\n    37\t  mode?: ValueMode,\n    38\t  included?: (row: number) => boolean,\n    39\t  outcome?: string,\n    40\t  counts?: ValueCounts,\n    41\t): Values {\n    42\t  const column = table.columns?.[field.field];\n    43\t  const borrowed = column instanceof Float64Array || column instanceof Float32Array;\n    44\t  const zero = impute && field.missing === 'zero';\n    45\t  const slot = new Uint8Array(table.length);\n    46\t  let y = borrowed ? column : new Float64Array(table.length);\n    47\t  let i = 0;\n    48\t  if (borrowed && !included) {\n    49\t    // Values and typed NaNs can stay in the caller's storage without generic row validation.\n    50\t    let missing = 0;\n    51\t    for (; i < table.length; i++) {\n    52\t      const value = column[i]!;\n    53\t      if (Number.isFinite(value)) continue;\n    54\t      if (zero || !Number.isNaN(value)) break;\n    55\t      slot[i] = SLOT_NULL;\n    56\t      missing++;\n    57\t    }\n    58\t    if (counts) counts.other += i - missing;\n    59\t    if (i === table.length) return { y, slot };\n    60\t  }\n    61\t  const reports = new Reports(field.field, sink);\n    62\t  mode ??= borrowed ? 'other' : inspectValues(table, field.field, included);\n     3\t{\"type\":\"turn.started\"}\n     4\t{\"type\":\"item.completed\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_1\",\"type\":\"agent_message\",\"text\":\"I’ll read `data.json` and the local Axylo docs, then write `chart.js` and run the documented Node checks.\"}}\n     5\t{\"type\":\"item.started\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_2\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/bin/bash -lc \\\"rg -n --glob 'AGENTS.md' . /tmp/axylo-rehearsal-6SKmnr/workspace/AGENTS.md /tmp/axylo-rehearsal-6SKmnr/AGENTS.md /tmp/AGENTS.md /AGENTS.md\\\"\",\"aggregated_output\":\"\",\"exit_code\":null,\"status\":\"in_progress\"}}\n     6\t{\"type\":\"item.completed\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_2\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/bin/bash -lc \\\"rg -n --glob 'AGENTS.md' . /tmp/axylo-rehearsal-6SKmnr/workspace/AGENTS.md /tmp/axylo-rehearsal-6SKmnr/AGENTS.md /tmp/AGENTS.md /AGENTS.md\\\"\",\"aggregated_output\":\"rg: /tmp/axylo-rehearsal-6SKmnr/workspace/AGENTS.md: No such file or directory (os error 2)\\nrg: /tmp/axylo-rehearsal-6SKmnr/AGENTS.md: No such file or directory (os error 2)\\nrg: /tmp/AGENTS.md: No such file or directory (os error 2)\\nrg: /AGENTS.md: No such file or directory (os error 2)\\n\",\"exit_code\":2,\"status\":\"failed\"}}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
