he chart in its error state when the ignored option was needed to draw at all (a `y` list on a scatter chart, [AX150](diagnostics.md#ax150)); and some hints come with a visible change: an inferred missing step is drawn as a gap ([AX105](diagnostics.md#ax105)), a plot too small to draw is replaced by its summary ([AX142](diagnostics.md#ax142)), hidden labels get a note ([AX143](diagnostics.md#ax143)).\napps/docs/pages/diagnostics.md:38:  level: 'error' | 'warning' | 'hint';\napps/docs/pages/diagnostics.md:57:`strict: true` makes the chart throw on any error or warning found while checking a create, `update` or `append` call, synchronously from that call. The chart keeps its last valid state; a rejected create leaves nothing in the page. The error is named `AxyloStrictError`, and its `diagnostics` property has every diagnostic of the rejected call. Hints never throw, and neither do diagnostics found later while drawing. A failure while a call is being checked (such as a row getter that throws, [AX199](diagnostics.md#ax199)) rejects that call too, with AX199 after what it had found; a failure later, while drawing, is never thrown. Each code's page says whether a strict chart throws it. See the example in [Updating](updating.md#strict-mode).\napps/docs/examples/node/validate.ts:17:// Errors and warnings mean something will not be drawn as given; hints are advice.\napps/docs/examples/node/validate.ts:18:const blocking = problems.filter(d => d.level !== 'hint');\n5:## When to use it\n13:## Options\n17:bar(target, { data, x, y, series, layout: 'grouped', horizontal: false, ...options });\n24:| `layout` | `'grouped'` (default) puts the series side by side; `'stacked'` stacks them. |\n33:## How a bar chart behaves\n41:| Missing values | A missing bar (a `null` or absent value, or a step Axylo infers is missing) gets a small \"no data\" mark, distinct from a zero bar: at the baseline for grouped bars, at the edge of the stack for stacked ones. A slot a series simply has no row for, as for a weekly series beside daily ones, gets no bar and no mark. |\n48:## Horizontal and grouped bars\n50:Long category names read best down the side. With two value fields the bars are grouped, and a missing value is a \"no data\" mark, not an empty slot that looks like zero.\n54:## Edge case: stacks with both signs\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
