ent' \\| 'ratio'` | none | Percentage data: `'percent'` is 0–100, `'ratio'` is 0–1. Never inferred. |\n   140\t| `format` | `Intl.NumberFormatOptions \\| ((value: number) => string)` | the locale's grouping, the full integer part and up to six significant fraction digits | How values are written in tooltip, table and announcements. |\n   141\t| `tickFormat` | `Intl.NumberFormatOptions \\| ((value: number) => string)` | the locale's grouping, with the step's fraction digits; compact from a largest tick of one million, scientific from 10¹⁵ | How axis ticks are written. |\n   142\t| `missing` | `'gap' \\| 'zero'` | `'gap'` | What a missing value means. `'zero'` is for counts where absence means none. |\n   116\t    code: 'AX106', level: 'warning', title: 'Values that are not numbers',\n   117\t    condition: 'A value field mixes numbers with strings, or holds strings that are not plain decimals (`\\'1,234\\'`, `\\'n/a\\'`). Also any other non-number value (`true`). The rule is field-wide: once one value is a number or a non-decimal, every string in the field is rejected, plain decimals included.', drawn: 'The strings are not drawn.',\n   118\t    see: 'Those values are left out (gaps), the reader sees \"Values not shown: 1. See table.\", and the console lists the rows and the values.',\n   119\t    why: 'A stray string in a column of numbers is a bug somewhere upstream. Strings such as `\\'1,234\\'` or `\\'n/a\\'` depend on a locale or a convention Axylo cannot know, so it does not guess, and it does not convert half a field.',\n   120\t    fix: 'Convert the values to numbers where the data is produced. For a field that is entirely plain decimal strings, use `parse: \\'number\\'` (see [AX104](diagnostics.md#ax104)).',\n   121\t    run: 'node',\n   122\t    input: `validate('line', {\n   123\t  title: 'Sessions',\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
