{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_53","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"nl -ba apps/docs/pages/diagnostics.md | sed -n '19,54p'\nnl -ba apps/docs/dist/options.html | sed -n '51,59p' | cut -c1-125\nnl -ba rehearsal/records/release-1e93128/*-codex-daily-revenue-3-*/transcript.jsonl | sed -n '26,38p' | cut -c1-185\nnl -ba apps/docs/pages/options.md | tail -48\"","aggregated_output":"    19\t## Levels and who is told\n    20\t\n    21\t| Level | Means | Console |\n    22\t|---|---|---|\n    23\t| Error | Something cannot be drawn as given: the chart, a series, or the donut. | Every build, once per code per page, with `console.warn` |\n    24\t| Warning | Something is not drawn as given, or an option is ignored. | Every build, once per code per page, with `console.warn` |\n    25\t| Hint | Advice for you. | Development builds only, with `console.info` |\n    26\t\n    27\tThe level says who is told; it does not by itself say what stays on screen. That depends on the code, and each code's page says it, with a checked minimal input. For example: an error about one series ([AX108](diagnostics.md#ax108)) leaves the other series drawn; a warning can put the chart in its error state when the ignored option was needed to draw at all (a `y` list on a scatter chart, [AX150](diagnostics.md#ax150)); and some hints come with a visible change: an inferred missing step is drawn as a gap ([AX105](diagnostics.md#ax105)), a plot too small to draw is replaced by its summary ([AX142](diagnostics.md#ax142)), hidden labels get a note ([AX143](diagnostics.md#ax143)).\n    28\t\n    29\tWhen values were left out or changed, the chart shows the reader a note in the figure (\"Values not shown: 3. See table.\", or \"Values shown differently from the data\"), in every build, and in the accessibility tree.\n    30\t\n    31\t## Collecting them in your code\n    32\t\n    33\tEach diagnostic is an object:\n    34\t\n    35\t```ts\n    36\tinterface Diagnostic {\n    37\t  code: `AX${number}`;           // 'AX103'\n    38\t  level: 'error' | 'warning' | 'hint';\n    39\t  message: string;               // what is wrong, where, and how to fix it\n    40\t  chart: string;                 // the chart's title, else its element id\n    41\t  field?: string;                // when it is about a field\n    42\t  rows?: readonly number[];      // first rows, in your data, at most 10\n    43\t  count?: number;                // how many values or rows in all\n    44\t}\n    45\t```\n    46\t\n    47\t`chart.diagnostics` lists them for the current options and data, up to date as soon as a create, `update` or `append` returns. `onDiagnostic` is called once for each diagnostic the chart newly finds, in every build and at every level, so it is the place to send them to your error tracking. A listener that throws is reported once and otherwise ignored; it cannot break the chart.\n    48\t\n    49\t[example: diagnostics-listener](../examples/diagnostics-listener.html)\n    50\t\n    51\t## When they are found\n    52\t\n    53\tMost diagnostics are found while a call checks its input: the create, `update` or `append` call. Those are in `chart.diagnostics` when the call returns. A few can only be found later, while drawing: low contrast after the page's CSS changes ([AX141](diagnostics.md#ax141)), a plot too small ([AX142](diagnostics.md#ax142)), labels that stop fitting after a resize ([AX143](diagnostics.md#ax143)), more bars than pixels ([AX132](diagnostics.md#ax132)), a formatter that fails ([AX160](diagnostics.md#ax160)), a `labelledBy` that names no element when there is no `title` ([AX140](diagnostics.md#ax140)), and an internal failure ([AX199](diagnostics.md#ax199)). They are reported when found, through the same console line and `onDiagnostic`. A `zoom()` call that cannot apply (a category axis, a donut, a compact chart) is reported when it is made, through the console line and `onDiagnostic` only: it changes nothing, so `chart.diagnostics` does not list it ([AX150](diagnostics.md#ax150)).\n    54\t\n    51\t<div class=\"table-scroll\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"Table: Scatter options\"><table><thead><tr><th scope=\"\n    52\t<h2 id=\"donut-options\">Donut options</h2>\n    53\t<div class=\"table-scroll\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"Table: Donut options\"><table><thead><tr><th scope=\"co\n    54\t<h2 id=\"value-fields\">Value fields</h2>\n    55\t<p>A value field is a key of <code>Row</code> whose values are numbers (or <code>null</code>), or an object. A key who\n    56\t<div class=\"table-scroll\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"Table: Value fields\"><table><thead><tr><th scope=\"col\n    57\t<h2 id=\"x-fields\">X fields</h2>\n    58\t<p>An x field is a key of <code>Row</code> whose values are numbers, strings or <code>Date</code>s, or an object.</p>\n    59\t<div class=\"table-scroll\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"Table: X fields\"><table><thead><tr><th scope=\"col\">Ke\n    26\t{\"type\":\"item.completed\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_12\",\"type\":\"file_change\",\"changes\":[{\"path\":\"/tmp/axylo-rehearsal-6SKmnr/workspace/chart.js\",\"kind\":\"add\"}],\"status\":\"completed\"}}\n    27\t{\"type\":\"item.started\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_13\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/bin/bash -lc 'node --experimental-permission --allow-fs-read=\\\"$PWD\\\" --input-type=module <<'\n    28\t{\"type\":\"item.completed\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_13\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/bin/bash -lc 'node --experimental-permission --allow-fs-read=\\\"$PWD\\\" --input-type=module <\n    29\t{\"type\":\"item.started\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_14\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/bin/bash -lc 'cat node_modules/axylo/package.json'\",\"aggregated_output\":\"\",\"exit_code\":null,\"\n    30\t{\"type\":\"item.started\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_15\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/bin/bash -lc 'rg --files --hidden --no-ignore node_modules/axylo'\",\"aggregated_output\":\"\",\"ex\n    31\t{\"type\":\"item.completed\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_14\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/bin/bash -lc 'cat node_modules/axylo/package.json'\",\"aggregated_output\":\"{\\n  \\\"name\\\": \\\"a\n    32\t{\"type\":\"item.completed\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_15\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/bin/bash -lc 'rg --files --hidden --no-ignore node_modules/axylo'\",\"aggregated_output\":\"nod\n    33\t{\"type\":\"item.started\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_16\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/bin/bash -lc \\\"rg -n -i -M 550 'child_process|node:fs|node:net|process\\\\\\\\.(binding|env|mainM\n    34\t{\"type\":\"item.completed\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_16\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/bin/bash -lc \\\"rg -n -i -M 550 'child_process|node:fs|node:net|process\\\\\\\\.(binding|env|mai\n    35\t{\"type\":\"item.started\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_17\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/bin/bash -lc 'cat chart.js'\",\"aggregated_output\":\"\",\"exit_code\":null,\"status\":\"in_progress\"}}\n    36\t{\"type\":\"item.completed\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_17\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/bin/bash -lc 'cat chart.js'\",\"aggregated_output\":\"import { line } from 'axylo';\\n\\nexport d\n    37\t{\"type\":\"item.started\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_18\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/bin/bash -lc \\\"node --input-type=module <<'NODE'\\nimport assert from 'node:assert/strict';\\ni\n    38\t{\"type\":\"item.completed\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_18\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/bin/bash -lc \\\"node --input-type=module <<'NODE'\\nimport assert from 'node:assert/strict';\\\n   197\t### Events\n   198\t\n   199\t<!-- options: ChartEvents -->\n   200\t| Event | Type | Meaning |\n   201\t|---|---|---|\n   202\t| `hover` | `Point<Row> \\| null` | The datum under the pointer or the keyboard's point; `null` when nothing is picked. |\n   203\t| `select` | `Point<Row>` | The reader clicked a point, or pressed Enter or Space on it. |\n   204\t| `zoom` | `readonly [XValue, XValue] \\| null` | A `zoom()` call or the reader changed the visible range; `null` for the whole range. Not sent when the view moves with appended data. |\n   205\t\n   206\t<!-- options: Point -->\n   207\t| Point key | Type | Meaning |\n   208\t|---|---|---|\n   209\t| `series` | `string` | The series key: the `series` value for long rows, the field name for wide rows, the slice label on a donut. |\n   210\t| `x` | `XValue` | In the form `zoom()` accepts: a `Date` for an instant, `'YYYY-MM-DD'` for a calendar date, an ISO date-time without offset for a wall-clock time, the category, otherwise the number. |\n   211\t| `y` | `number \\| null` | The value; `null` for no data. |\n   212\t| `row` | `Row \\| null` | Your row; with typed columns, an object built from the columns at that index; `null` for a position no row holds. |\n   213\t| `index` | `number` | The row's index in your data; `-1` when `row` is `null`. |\n   214\t\n   215\t### Diagnostic\n   216\t\n   217\t<!-- options: Diagnostic -->\n   218\t| Key | Type | Meaning |\n   219\t|---|---|---|\n   220\t| `code` | `` `AX${number}` `` | Stable code, with a page under [Diagnostics](diagnostics.md). |\n   221\t| `level` | `'error' \\| 'warning' \\| 'hint'` | See [levels](diagnostics.md#levels-and-who-is-told). |\n   222\t| `message` | `string` | What is wrong, where, and how to fix it. |\n   223\t| `chart` | `string` | The chart's title, else its element id. |\n   224\t| `field` | `string` | The field or option, when it is about one. |\n   225\t| `rows` | `readonly number[]` | The first offending rows in your data, at most ten, when it is about rows. |\n   226\t| `count` | `number` | How many values or rows in all, when it counts them. |\n   227\t\n   228\t## validate\n   229\t\n   230\t`validate(type, options)` takes `'line'`, `'area'`, `'bar'`, `'scatter'` or `'donut'` and that type's options, runs the checks a created chart runs from its call without a DOM, and returns `Diagnostic[]`. It cannot find what needs a page: contrast, sizes, label fitting, formatters, or whether a `labelledBy` id exists. See [Diagnostics](diagnostics.md#validate-in-node-and-in-tests).\n   231\t\n   232\t## Messages\n   233\t\n   234\tEvery message the chart shows the reader can be replaced through `messages`: the notes, states, controls, the table's labels, the generated name and summary. Diagnostics for developers keep the registry's English wording. Placeholders in braces are filled in by the chart; an override should keep the ones it needs. `{seeTable}` is filled with `seeTable` when the chart has a table and removed when it does not (`table: false`), so a translated note that keeps it reads right either way:\n   235\t\n   236\t[example: messages-translated](../examples/messages-translated.ts)\n   237\t\n   238\tEvery key, with its built-in English text, read from the library when this site is built, and where the chart shows it:\n   239\t\n   240\t[table: messages](../../../packages/axylo/src/messages/index.ts)\n   241\t\n   242\t## Options that do not exist\n   243\t\n   244\tThere is no `width`, `height`, `responsive`, `theme`, `palette` or `animation` option. Size comes from the container, colours from [CSS](theming.md), and motion from the reader's settings: the first render is not animated, and nothing moves under reduced motion. Each of these names, like any unknown key, is ignored with [AX150](diagnostics.md#ax150), which suggests the closest known option.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
